%T A398534 0,9,0,2,1,4,3,3,0,3,7,5,9,6,3,3,2,2,0,1,9,2,6,0,3,4,0,4,3,0,3,1,9,2,
%U A398534 2,8,3,5,9,2,8,2,8,6,4,6,3,3,8,2,7,3,5,3,6,2,5,5,0,5,5,2,6,6,2,1,6,1,2,2,5
%N A398534 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} phi(k)/(k^2*(k+1)), where phi is the Euler totient function.
%C A398534 This constant appears in the asymptotic formula for the function A398532(n)/A398533(n).
%H A398534 Olivier Bordellès, Lixia Dai, Randell Heyman, Hao Pan, and Igor E. Shparlinski, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jnt.2019.01.006">On a sum involving the Euler function</a>, Journal of Number Theory, Vol. 202 (2019), pp. 278-297.
%H A398534 Shane Chern, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1017/S0004972719000066">Note on sums involving the Euler function</a>, Bulletin of the Australian Mathematical Society, Vol. 100, No. 2 (2019), pp. 194-200.
%H A398534 Jing Ma and Huayan Sun, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.02924">On a sum involving certain arithmetic functions and the integral part function</a>, arXiv:2109.02924 [math.NT], 2021.
%H A398534 Jie Wu, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s10998-019-00300-6">Note on a paper by Bordellès, Dai, Heyman, Pan and Shparlinski</a>, Periodica Mathematica Hungarica, Vol. 80, (2020), pp. 95-102.
%H A398534 Guang-Liang Zhou and Ya-Fang Feng, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1216/rmj.2024.54.623">Distribution of the Primes Represented by floor(x/n) in Short Intervals</a>, Rocky Mountain Journal of Mathematics, Vol. 54, No. 2 (2024), pp. 623-629.
%F A398534 Equals 1/2 + Sum_{k>=3} (-1)^k * (D(k) - 1), where D(s) = zeta(s-1)/zeta(s) is the Dirichlet g.f. of phi.
%e A398534 0.788385435416730381148604108858102609021433037596332...
%o A398534 (PARI) suminf(k = 3, (-1)^(k+1) * (zeta(k-1) / zeta(k) - 1)) + 1/2
%Y A398534 Cf. A000010, A398532, A398533.
%K A398534 nonn,cons,new
%O A398534 0,1
%A A398534 _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 01 2026
